  "description": "This creamy parsnip soup recipe, inspired by Thai tom kha, is made with coconut milk, lemongrass, galangal (or ginger), and makrut lime leaves. It's comforting enough for winter but light and bright enough to take you into spring.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: yellow onion → white onion; galangal → ginger; homemade chicken stock → store-bought unsalted chicken or vegetable broth\n\nNotes: Galangal, lemongrass, and makrut lime leaves can be found at many Asian grocery stores.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days or frozen for up to 2 months.",
